\pxt3.001,3.999,5.999;1.^IALL EXTERIOR HEADERS ABOVE OPENINGS SHALL BE 6 x 10 #1 DF ^IUNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED. INTERIOR HEADER SHALL BE 4 x 8 #2 DF ^IUNLESS NOTED.\P2.^IALL INTERIOR PLUMBING WALLS RECOMMENDED TO BE 2 x 6 STUDS ^I@ 16" O.C.\P3.^IPROVIDE FIRE
  3
 STOPS IN CONCEALED SPACES OF STUD WALLS ^IINCLUDING SPACES AT CEILINGS AND FLOORS AND IN OPENINGS ^IAROUND DUCTS, PIPES. CHIMNEYS AND SIMILAR OPENINGS WHICH ^IALLOW PASSAGE OF FIRE.\P4.^ISHOWER AREA WALLS SHALL BE FINISHED WITH A SMOOTH ^INON-ABSORBENT. 
  3
HARD SURFACE TO A HEIGHT OF 70" ABOVE DRAIN ^IINLET.\P5.^IALL FIREPLACES SHALL HAVE APPROVED COLLAPSIBLE METAL OR ^IGLASS DOORS AND OUTSIDE COMBUSTION AIR. OUTSIDE ^ICOMBUSTION AIR IS NOT REQUIRED ON INTERIOR FIREPLACES ^IINSTALLED OVER CONCRETE SLAB ON G
  3
RADE. MANUFACTURER'S ^IINSTALLATION GUIDE TO BE ON-SITE FOR INSPECTION.\P6.^IALL SOLID FUEL BURNING APPLIANCES (STOVES/FIREPLACES) FOR ^IWHICH A CONSTRUCTION PERMIT APPLICATION IS SUBMITTED AFTER ^IFEBRUARY 1,1994 MAY BE INSTALLED ONLY IF "EPA" CERTIFIED
  3
 AS ^IRECOGNIZED BY THE AIR POLLUTION CONTROL BOARD (COUNTY ^IBOARD OF SUPERVISOR) ACPD 504.\P7.^IFLUE DAMPER TO BE PERMANENTLY BLOCKED OPEN IF A GAS LOG ^ILIGHTER IS PROPOSED. CMC\P8.^IFLOOR LEVEL CHANGE AT DOORS NOT TO EXCEED {\H0.7x;1#2}".\P9.^IMETAL CH
  3
IMNEYS SHALL BE ANCHORED AT EACH FLOOR AND ROOF ^IWITH TWO 1 ½" x 1/8" METAL STRAPS LOOPED AROUND THE OUTSIDE ^IOF THE CHIMNEY INSTALLATION AND NAILED WITH NOT LESS THAN ^I(6) 8d NAILS PER STRAP AT EACH JOIST. CBC\P10.^IPROVIDE EMERGENCY EXIT DOOR OR WIN
  3
DOW FROM SLEEPING ^IROOMS. NET CLEAR WINDOW OPENING SHALL NOT BE LESS THAN 5.0 ^ISQ. FT. MIN. NET OPENING HEIGHT DIMENSION, 24" CLEAR; MIN. NET ^IOPENING WIDTH DIMENSION, 20" CLEAR FINISHED SILL HEIGHT. MAX. ^I44" TO THE BOTTOM OF THE CLEAR OPENING.\P11.
  3
^IOCCUPANCY SEPARATION BETWEEN GARAGE AND HOUSE SHALL BE ^IOF {\H0.7x;1#2}" GYPSUM BOARD CONSTRUCTION ON THE GARAGE SIDE. CBC\P^I^IA.^IFIREWALL IS REQUIRED TO EXTEND FROM FLOOR TO  ROOF ^I^I^I^ISHEATHING PROVIDED A COMPLETE SEPARATION BETWEEN THE ^I^I^IGARAGE AN
  3
D SFD OR THE CEILING AND ALL  BEARING WALLS OF ^I^I^ICEILING ARE REQUIRED TO BE COVERED WITH FIRE RATED ^I^I^I^I^IDRYWALL.\P^I^I^IB.^IWHEN THE CEILING IN THE GARAGE IS REQUIRED TO BE  ^I^I^I^IENTIRELY PROTECTED, THE WALLS, BEAMS OR POSTS ^I^I^I^I^I^ISUPPORTING THE CEILING
  3
 ARE TO BE PROTECTED WITH  ^I^I^I^I^IEQUIVALENT FIRE RESTRICTIVE CONSTRUCTION. CBC\P^I^I^IC.^IIF THE SEPARATION IS A FLOOR-CEILING ASSEMBLY. THE  ^I^I^I^ICEILING AND ALL SUPPORTING ELEMENTS AND POSTS MUST BE ^I^I^I^IFIRE PROTECTED AND JACKETED FOR  PROTECTION AGAINST
  3
 ^I^I^I^IMECHANICAL DAMAGE 704.2.5 AND 6.\P^I^I^I12.^ISKYLIGHTS SHALL BE TEMPERED GLASS.\P^I^I^I13.^IEXTERIOR WINDOWS, WINDOW WALLS, GLAZED DOORS, AND ^I^I^IGLAZED  DOORS SHALL BE DUAL-GLAZED UNITS WITH A MINIMUM ^I^I^IOF ONE TEMPERED PANE OR SHALL BE GLOSS BLOCK UNIT
  3
S OR ^I^I^ISHALL HAVE A FIRE-RESTRICTIVE RATING NOT LESS THAN 20 ^I^I^I^IMINUTES. GLAZING FRAMES MADE OF VINYL SHALL HAVE ^I^I^I^I^IWELDED CORNERS AND METAL REINFORCEMENT IN THE ^I^I^I^I^IINTERLOCK AREA.\P^I^I^I14.^IEXTERIOR DOORS AND EXTERIOR GLAZING SHALL COMPLY ^I^I^I^IWI
  1
TH FIRE REQUIREMENTS PER SHEET WF-1.
